# Every text file is LF in the repository and in every checkout. Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true, and a clone made that way (2026-10-10) had
# CRLF everywhere: the build no longer matched the committed page, the --cdn rewrite could not find
# its sentence, and three suites failed on a stranger's first `npm test`. The two fixtures are bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf
tools/fixtures/*.block0 binary
tools/fixtures/*.wtproj binary

# The two third-party libraries in src/vendor/ are pinned to the bytes cdnjs's SRI hashes name, and
# tools/t41_build.mjs checks that on every `npm test` (ROADMAP 4.50 (1)). A checkout that rewrote
# their line endings — Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true — would hand the build, and
# the check, different bytes from the pin. `-text` leaves them exactly as committed.
src/vendor/three-r128.min.js -text
src/vendor/jszip-3.10.1.min.js -text
